A boat travels 30 km downstream in 2 hours and the same distance upstream in 3 hours. What is the speed of the boat in still water?

A) 10 km/h
B) 12 km/h
C) 12.5 km/h
D) 15 km/h

Answer: C) 12.5 km/h

Explanation:

Downstream speed:

$$ \frac{30}{2}=15\text{ km/h} $$

Upstream speed:

$$ \frac{30}{3}=10\text{ km/h} $$

Speed of boat in still water:

$$ \frac{\text{Downstream speed}+\text{Upstream speed}}{2} $$
=
2
15+10
	​

=
12.5 km/h
	​
